When the buffer becomes full, it is flushed to the cache service (in this case, an external caching service) using the `CacheService` module. If the cache service is temporarily unavailable, the logs are written to disk for potential replay or analysis. The system also includes a fallback mechanism that writes logs to disk in case of persistent cache failures.

The implementation is optimized for concurrent processing by allowing for parallel log parsing and transformation tasks using `Promise` and `async/await`. The system uses the `ThreadSafe` module to ensure thread-safety and handle a high volume of concurrent requests without significant performance degradation.

An API endpoint is provided to trigger a manual flush of the buffered logs to the cache or disk using the `EventEmitter` API. Robust error handling and logging are implemented using the `console.error()` function, and system performance is monitored using the `performance` module. The system also includes instructions for testing the system under load."]

