```
public class MoSTState {
    private int maxThreads;
    private List<String> tasks;
    private Map<String, TaskStatus> taskStatuses;

    public MoSTState(int maxThreads) {
        this.maxThreads = maxThreads;
        this.tasks = new ArrayList<>();
        this.taskStatuses = new HashMap<>();
    }

    public void addTask(String taskName, TaskStatus status) {
        tasks.add(taskName);
        taskStatuses.put(taskName, status);
    }

    public void removeTask(String taskName) {
        tasks.remove(taskName);
        taskStatuses.remove(taskName);
    }

    public TaskStatus getTaskStatus(String taskName) {
        return taskStatuses.get(taskName);
    }
}
```
This class defines a `MoSTState` object that has a maximum number of threads, a list of tasks, and a map of task names to their current statuses. It also provides methods for adding or removing tasks, and getting the status of a specific task by its name.']

