### 2.1 Encryption and Decryption using DES Algorithm
In this section, we will implement the functions for encryption and decryption of data using the DES algorithm.
The DES (Data Encryption Standard) is a block cipher that uses a 56-bit key for encrypting/decrypting data. It has been widely used in various applications due to its security and efficiency. The DES algorithm uses a Feistel structure, which consists of two main components: encryption and decryption.
The encryption process involves splitting the plaintext into sixteen 64-bit blocks and applying a series of bit operations on each block using a round function. After all the bits have been operated upon by the round function, the final result is obtained by adding a constant to the plaintext and performing a modulo operation with respect to 2^31. The decryption process is similar to the encryption process except that it involves applying a series of bit operations in reverse order to each block using the inverse of the round function.
Here are the implementations of the functions for encrypting/decrypting data using DES algorithm:
```java
// Encrypts the input text using DES Algorithm
public static byte[] encrypt(byte[] plainText, byte[] key) {
  return cryptography.des.encrypt(plainText, key);
}

// Decrypts the input ciphertext using DES Algorithm
public static byte[] decrypt(byte[] cipherText, byte[] key) {
  return cryptography.des.decrypt(cipherText, key);
}
```
The encrypt and decrypt functions take in two parameters: plainText and key. The plainText is the input data that needs to be encrypted/decrypted, and the key is used for encryption/decryption. The encrypt function returns the ciphertext obtained by applying the DES algorithm on the plainText using the key, while the decrypt function returns the original plaintext after applying the inverse of the round function on the ciphertext using the same key that was used during encryption.
### 2.2 Encryption and Decryption using AES Algorithm
AES (Advanced Encryption Standard) is a symmetric block cipher that uses a variable-length key. It has been widely adopted in various applications due to its security and efficiency. The AES algorithm uses a Feistel structure, which consists of two main components: encryption and decryption.
The encryption process involves splitting the plaintext into n blocks and applying a series of bit operations on each block using a round function. After all the bits have been operated upon by the round function, the final result is obtained by adding a constant to the plaintext and performing a modulo operation with respect to 2^8n. The decryption process is similar to the encryption process except that it involves applying a series of bit operations in reverse order to each block using the inverse of the round function.
Here are the implementations of the functions for encrypting/decrypting data using AES algorithm:
```java
// Encrypts the input text using AES Algorithm
public static byte[] encrypt(byte[] plainText, byte[] key) {
  return cryptography.aes.encrypt(plainText, key);
}

// Decrypts the input ciphertext using AES Algorithm
public static byte[] decrypt(byte[] cipherText, byte[] key) {
  return cryptography.aes.decrypt(cipherText, key);
}
```
The encrypt and decrypt functions take in two parameters: plainText and key. The plainText is the input data that needs to be encrypted/decrypted, and the key is used for encryption/decryption. The encrypt function returns the ciphertext obtained by applying the AES algorithm on the plainText using the key, while the decrypt function returns the original plaintext after applying the inverse of the round function on the ciphertext using the same key that was used during encryption.
### 2.3 Encryption and Decryption using RSA Algorithm
RSA (Rivest-Shamir-Adleman) is a public-key algorithm used for encrypting/decrypting data over an insecure channel. It uses two large prime numbers to construct the keys, one private key and one public key. The private key can be used to decrypt the message, while the public key can be used to encrypt the message.
Here are the implementations of the functions for encrypting/decrypting data using RSA algorithm:
```java
// Encrypts the input text using RSA Algorithm
public static byte[] encrypt(byte[] plainText, PublicKey publicKey) {
  return cryptography.rsa.encrypt(plainText, publicKey);
}

// Decrypts the input ciphertext using RSA Algorithm
public static byte[] decrypt(byte[] cipherText, PrivateKey privateKey) {
  return cryptography.rsa.decrypt(cipherText, privateKey);
}
```
The encrypt and decrypt functions take in two parameters: plainText and key. The plainText is the input data that needs to be encrypted/decrypted, and the key is used for encryption/decryption. The encrypt function returns the ciphertext obtained by applying the RSA algorithm on the plainText using the public key, while the decrypt function returns the original plaintext after applying the inverse of the round function on the ciphertext using the same private key that was used during encryption.
# 3. Conclusion
In this project, we have implemented an encryption and decryption tool using DES, AES, and RSA algorithms. The tool takes in two parameters: plainText and key. The plainText is the input data that needs to be encrypted/decrypted, and the key is used for encryption/decryption. The encrypt function returns the ciphertext obtained by applying the algorithm on the plainText using the key, while the decrypt function returns the original plaintext after applying the inverse of the round function on the ciphertext using the same key that was used during encryption.
The tool supports multiple algorithms including DES, AES, and RSA. The user can choose from among these algorithms to encrypt/decrypt their data as per their requirement.']

