The second Kafka Streams topology is defined using the `addSource()` method to read from a source topic named "market-data-stream", which contains the output of the first Kafka Streams topology. The `addProcessor()` method is then used to add a processor that performs advanced analytics and modeling on the market data, such as pattern recognition and predictive modeling, and sends the results to a sink topic named "analytics-results".

Finally, the `start()` method starts both Kafka Streams instances using the `build().start()` method.']

