    // Aggregate and store metrics
    std::vector<Metric> aggregatedMetrics = metricAggregator->aggregate();
    dataStorage->store(aggregatedMetrics);

    // Cache aggregated metrics for quick access
    caching->cache(aggregatedMetrics);
  }
}

void runProcessor() {
  while (true) {
    // Get cached aggregated metrics
    auto cachedMetrics = caching->get();

    // Process and analyze cached metrics
    for (const auto& metric : cachedMetrics) {
      metricProcessor->process(metric);
    }
  }
}

void runStorage() {
  while (true) {
    // Get stored aggregated metrics from data storage
    auto storedMetrics = dataStorage->load();

    // Analyze and visualize stored metrics
    for (const auto& metric : storedMetrics) {
      logging->log(metric);
      visualization->visualize(metric);
    }
  }
}

int main() {
  // Initialize services
  networkService = std::make_shared<NetworkService>(oauth2);
  metricAggregator = std::make_shared<MetricAggregator>();
  dataStorage = std::make_shared<DataStorage>();
  caching = std::make_shared<Caching>(CACHE_SIZE);
  logging = std::make_shared<Logging>();
  visualization = std::make_shared<Visualization>();

  // Start collector thread
  threads.push_back(std::thread(runCollector));

  // Start processor thread
  threads.push_back(std::thread(runProcessor));

  // Start storage thread
  threads.push_back(std::thread(runStorage));

  // Wait for all threads to finish
  for (auto& t : threads) {
    t.join();
  }

  return 0;
}
```
This is a basic implementation of the `networkMetricsCollector` library that includes the necessary functionalities for monitoring and aggregating key performance metrics from distributed network services, providing real-time insights and historical data analytics. The library is designed to integrate seamlessly with various monitoring tools and cloud platforms, ensuring compatibility across different deployment environments.

The implementation decisions made for this library include the use of a custom memory pool and thread pool to manage resources efficiently, the integration of OAuth 2.0 authentication for secure API access, and the use of caching mechanisms to reduce API calls and improve performance. The library also includes a custom logging framework to capture errors and report them without disrupting normal operations.

The operational constraints of this library include supporting scaling across multiple nodes in a Kubernetes cluster, handling stateless and stateful data streams, and ensuring seamless integration with microservices architecture. The library is designed to handle large volumes of data in real-time, optimizing for low latency and high throughput.

Overall, this implementation provides a modular and extensible C++ library for monitoring and aggregating key performance metrics from distributed network services, providing real-time insights and historical data analytics. The library is designed to integrate seamlessly with various monitoring tools and cloud platforms, ensuring compatibility across different deployment environments.']

