The encryption mechanism used is AES-256 in CBC mode with GCM, which provides authentication tags for message integrity verification. The key length is set to 32 bytes (256 bits), and the IV length is set to 16 bytes (128 bits). The tag length is also set to 16 bytes (128 bits) for GCM mode.

The encryption and decryption functions use the EVP_EncryptInit(), EVP_EncryptUpdate(), EVP_EncryptFinal() and EVP_DecryptInit(), EVP_DecryptUpdate(), and EVP_DecryptFinal() OpenSSL APIs to perform the encryption and decryption operations.

The code also includes error handling using the ERR_get_error() and ERR_error_string() functions from OpenSSL. These functions provide a way to check for errors in the library and retrieve their corresponding error messages.

In addition, the code includes some performance optimization techniques such as using EVP_CIPHER_CTX_ctrl() to set the key and IV lengths, and using EVP_EncryptUpdate() and EVP_DecryptUpdate() APIs to encrypt and decrypt the message in chunks instead of all at once.']

