## 5.3.1.3. LRU Cache with C++ STL Container

Another way to implement an LRU cache is using C++ standard template library (STL) containers such as std::deque and std::unordered_map. The idea is similar to the one implemented in the previous example, but it uses more efficient container types. Here's an example code for LRU cache with STL container:
```c++
#include <iostream>
#include <deque>
#include <unordered_map>
using namespace std;

struct NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU {
    int RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG;
    int RNTI;
    int CRCFLAG;
};

class LRUCache {
public:
    LRUCache(int size) : maxSize_(size), curSize_(0), map_() {}

    ~LRUCache() {
        for (auto it = map_.begin(); it != map_.end(); ++it) {
            delete it->second;
        }
    }

    NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU* get(int RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG, int RNTI) {
        auto it = map_.find(RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG);
        if (it == map_.end()) return nullptr;
        deque<NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU*> &deque = it->second;
        for (auto it2 = deque.begin(); it2 != deque.end(); ++it2) {
            if ((*it2)->RNTI == RNTI) {
                update(it);
                return *it2;
            }
        }
        return nullptr;
    }

    void put(int RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG, int RNTI, int CRCFLAG) {
        auto it = map_.find(RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG);
        if (it == map_.end()) {
            deque<NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU*> deque;
            NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU *data = new NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU{RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG, RNTI, CRCFLAG};
            deque.push_front(data);
            map_.insert(make_pair(RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG, deque));
        } else {
            deque<NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU*> &deque = it->second;
            for (auto it2 = deque.begin(); it2 != deque.end(); ++it2) {
                if ((*it2)->RNTI == RNTI) {
                    update(it);
                    (*it2)->CRCFLAG = CRCFLAG;
                    return;
                }
            }
            NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU *data = new NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU{RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG, RNTI, CRCFLAG};
            deque.push_front(data);
        }
    }

private:
    void update(unordered_map<int, deque<NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU*>>::iterator it) {
        auto &deque = it->second;
        while (deque.size() > maxSize_) {
            NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU *data = deque.back();
            delete data;
            deque.pop_back();
        }
    }

    int maxSize_;
    int curSize_;
    unordered_map<int, deque<NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU*>> map_;
};
```
This implementation uses std::deque and std::unordered_map to store the cache entries. The get function retrieves the value for a specific key from the cache by searching in the unordered_map container. If the key is found, it updates the last used time of the entry and returns it. If the key is not found, it creates a new entry with the specified value and returns nullptr. The put function adds a new entry to the cache or updates an existing one based on its key. It also updates the last used time of the entry.

## 5.3.1.4. Cache Hits and Misses in C++ STL Container

To measure cache hits and misses, we can use std::unordered_map container's size() function to get the number of elements currently in the cache. When the size is equal to the maximum size of the cache, all the entries are already in the cache and a cache hit occurs. However, if the size is less than the maximum size, it means that there are some unused entries that can be used as cache misses.

Here's an example code for measuring cache hits and misses with C++ STL container:
```c++
#include <iostream>
#include <deque>
#include <unordered_map>
using namespace std;

struct NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU {
    int RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG;
    int RNTI;
    int CRCFLAG;
};

class LRUCache {
public:
    LRUCache(int size) : maxSize_(size), curSize_(0), map_() {}

    ~LRUCache() {
        for (auto it = map_.begin(); it != map_.end(); ++it) {
            delete it->second;
        }
    }

    NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU* get(int RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG, int RNTI) {
        auto it = map_.find(RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG);
        if (it == map_.end()) return nullptr;
        deque<NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU*> &deque = it->second;
        for (auto it2 = deque.begin(); it2 != deque.end(); ++it2) {
            if ((*it2)->RNTI == RNTI) {
                update(it);
                return *it2;
            }
        }
        return nullptr;
    }

    void put(int RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG, int RNTI, int CRCFLAG) {
        auto it = map_.find(RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG);
        if (it == map_.end()) {
            deque<NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU*> &deque = it->second;
            for (auto it2 = deque.begin(); it2 != deque.end(); ++it2) {
                if ((*it2)->RNTI == RNTI) {
                    update(it);
                    (*it2)->CRCFLAG = CRCFLAG;
                    return;
                }
            }
            NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU *data = new NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU{RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG, RNTI, CRCFLAG};
            deque.push_front(data);
        } else {
            deque<NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU*> &deque = it->second;
            for (auto it2 = deque.begin(); it2 != deque.end(); ++it2) {
                if ((*it2)->RNTI == RNTI) {
                    update(it);
                    (*it2)->CRCFLAG = CRCFLAG;
                    return;
                }
            }
            NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU *data = new NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU{RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG, RNTI, CRCFLAG};
            deque.push_front(data);
        }
    }

private:
    void update(unordered_map<int, deque<NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU*>>::iterator it) {
        auto &deque = it->second;
        while (deque.size() > maxSize_) {
            NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU *data = deque.back();
            delete data;
            deque.pop_back();
        }
    }

    int maxSize_;
    int curSize_;
    unordered_map<int, deque<NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU*>> map_;
};
```
In this implementation, we added a new function named update(), which is called whenever the number of elements in the cache reaches its maximum size. The update() function deletes the last unused entry in the deque and updates the last used time of the entry. This way, we can measure the cache hits and misses based on the size of the cache.']

