This is the class definition for `DynamicImageProcessor`, which handles the ingestion, transformation, and export of image batches from various storage locations while integrating with an external image processing service. The class supports dynamic data ingestion and validation, resource management and efficiency, a flexible transformation pipeline, performance optimization, concurrency and scalability, and export and format conversion.

The `DynamicImageProcessor` class has the following public methods:

* `addImages`: Adds images to the cache for processing. The method takes in a vector of image paths and a map of metadata as input.
* `processImages`: Processes the images in the cache. If the `synchronous` parameter is set to `true`, the method will block until all images are processed, otherwise it will return immediately after starting the processing thread.
