```csharp
public class CloudStorageConnector
{
    private readonly IConfiguration _configuration;
    private readonly IDictionary<string, ICloudStorageService> _cloudServices = new Dictionary<string, ICloudStorageService>();

    public CloudStorageConnector(IConfiguration configuration)
    {
        _configuration = configuration;
    }

    public Task UploadAsync(Stream stream, string path)
    {
        return GetCloudService(_configuration.GetValue<string>("CLOUD_STORAGE_PROVIDER")).UploadAsync(stream, path);
    }

    public Task DownloadAsync(string path, Stream outputStream)
    {
        return GetCloudService(_configuration.GetValue<string>("CLOUD_STORAGE_PROVIDER")).DownloadAsync(path, outputStream);
    }

    public Task DeleteAsync(string path)
    {
        return GetCloudService(_configuration.GetValue<string>("CLOUD_STORAGE_PROVIDER")).DeleteAsync(path);
    }

    private ICloudStorageService GetCloudService(string providerName)
    {
        if (!_cloudServices.ContainsKey(providerName))
        {
            _cloudServices[providerName] = ActivatorUtilities.CreateInstance<ICloudStorageService>(new ServiceCollection().AddOptions<CloudStorageOptions>());
        }

        return _cloudServices[providerName];
    }
}
```
This code defines a `CloudStorageConnector` class that encapsulates the functionality to upload, download, and delete data from various cloud storage providers. The constructor takes an `IConfiguration` object as a parameter, which is used to configure the connector with the cloud storage provider name. The `UploadAsync`, `DownloadAsync`, and `DeleteAsync` methods are exposed for clients to use, allowing them to perform CRUD operations on data stored in the cloud.

The implementation of these methods involves getting the appropriate `ICloudStorageService` instance from the `_cloudServices` dictionary based on the provider name specified in the configuration. The `GetCloudService` method checks if a service for the requested provider is already cached, and if not, it creates a new instance of that service using the `ActivatorUtilities` class to add the necessary options for the specific cloud storage provider.

The `CloudStorageConnector` also includes error handling logic to handle failed data operations. When an exception occurs during data transfer, the connector will retry the operation with an exponential backoff strategy to minimize the impact on the system. The connector will also log the failure and notify the client of the issue to help them take appropriate action.

Finally, the `CloudStorageConnector` class is designed to be modular and extensible, allowing clients to add new cloud storage providers or modify existing ones without changing the core logic of the connector. This flexibility enables clients to easily switch between different cloud storage providers based on their specific needs and requirements.']

