This method takes a byte array as input and attempts to deserialize it using the `ObjectInputStream` class. If the deserialization is successful, it returns an object of the specified type (i.e., `T`). If there is an error during deserialization, such as an invalid class or data corruption, the method throws a `RuntimeException` with a meaningful message.

